+## GPU ownership boundary
+
+The Rust API communicates only with the existing local GPU gateway at `127.0.0.1:11500`. The Python GPU Supervisor remains the sole authority for GPU leases, process lifecycle, and VRAM coordination. Rust must not call the upstream model server directly or acquire a second GPU lock.
+
 ## Scope and remaining work
 
-This is a working API foundation, not the complete autonomous DREAD platform. Production authentication/authorization, audit logging, migrations, agent adapters, plugin import, repair orchestration, GPU-supervisor integration, native installers, and full end-to-end hardware validation remain separate milestones. The GPU Supervisor must remain the sole GPU coordination authority.
+This is a working API foundation, not the complete autonomous DREAD platform. Production authentication/authorization, audit logging, database migrations, runtime agent adapters, a live capability/plugin registry, approval and repair orchestration, a complete frontend, native installers, and full end-to-end hardware validation remain separate milestones. The GPU Supervisor must remain the sole GPU coordination authority.
 
